# Master Engineering Standards (Language-Agnostic)
Accordex Systems Pvt Ltd / Softmerce Technologies

These rules apply to ALL code in ANY language. Language-specific rule files may
refine syntax conventions but must never weaken the security or quality
principles here.

## Prime directive
- Correctness and security come before speed of delivery. If a request would
  produce insecure code, implement the secure version and note it.
- Never invent APIs, fields, env vars, or table names. If unknown, leave a
  clearly marked `TODO:` explaining what is needed — do not guess silently.
- Prefer clarity over cleverness. Code is read far more often than written.
- Follow the existing project's conventions and structure before inventing new ones.

## Code quality
- One responsibility per function/class/module; keep functions short.
- DRY: extract shared logic instead of copy-pasting.
- Descriptive names; avoid deep nesting (prefer early returns / guard clauses).
- No dead code, leftover commented-out blocks, or debug prints in commits.
- Isolate side effects; keep logic pure where practical.

## When unsure
- State assumptions explicitly at the top of the response.
- Offer the secure/correct option even if a quicker one was requested.
- Ask a clarifying question only when a wrong guess would be costly; otherwise
  proceed with the safest reasonable default and flag it.
